INSERT INTO public.posts (id, user_id, title, description, content, is_draft, created_at, cover_image, table_of_contents) VALUES
  ('7b285776-0364-496d-806a-2c2848b42cf2', 'a3b3cf93-6956-41c7-bec0-13f95dd42f26', 'Let''s get started!', 'Let''s get started with this Angular app!  In the first chapter, we''ll create a new project, configure Firebase, and set everything up. The project will be built using Angular 18+ with SSG (Static Site Generation).  For hosting, we''ll use Firebase''s new App Hosting, specifically designed for SSG Angular apps.  Our goal is to create an app that will break records on Lighthouse-type benchmarks!', '<div><u style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">PRE:&nbsp;First of all, Create a github repo.&nbsp;</u></div><div></div><h1 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">CONCEPTION</span></h1><div class="ql-align-center"></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Ok, so in this article we will Create a Blog with Admin UI, using the new Angular 18 with SSG/SSR, Firebase with Firestore, Authentication </span><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">and the latest feature from Firestore </span><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">- App Hosting - especially created for SSG/SRR Angular App! That’s dope!</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Our goal is to create an app with pre rendered parts, for high scores in performance tools like Lighthouse and google SEO. This was achievable by Angular Universal but it has a bad DX. </span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">I also can use this new amazing thing - AnalogJS, but for me it is too far from Angular.</span></div><div></div><h1 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">LET’S GET STARTED</span></h1><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">First, we will create a new project on Firebase. If you don’t have an account- create one. Then go to:</span><a href="https://console.firebase.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://console.firebase.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Firebase Console</a></u></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcQPf1Lx6YemzDtmWD7bBQDTvje-lyjwP3HUpslNU2NjpNQ9l-aaEj5wApIu5W_RIdKbsVHHXEB7ROuW8cxUrPA9EWMKgqO3Coprewwv462FayYgyWk1jCzjEmpALaVSfy_qAi2UULj12pAs3PMC1ku5hJZ?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="292" width="334"></span></div><ul><li><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">I’ll call my project the ‘angularBlog’,</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">I agree with Google Analytics and continue,</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">I’ll choose my default account and create the project</span><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.</span></li></ul><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">We need to wait a minute for a new project to show up.</span></div><div></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcCujElVSZBom3bw7fwDrmFTjeqjj5kzlfVhcmrlRNyvLseGcELsraSBI9jgxk4tfI5sndlmRXoRnNNB_SNKPpP7pbyh4GGcs6woMJIFI_NfBr3vQVLdJBN8t43S9r2018otT8v37Sv7IuL5_8I7K2zJ_s?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="368" width="329"></span></div><div class="ql-align-center"></div><div class="ql-align-center"></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">It’s ready, so let’s continue. Now that we’re on our project dashboard, we’ll create a new app.</span></div><div></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfq8SLtQwh-CMqJPyDmolYAO0Q1SdCk1Deq0g3sh-bCBUXp8LSsJEySF315JNGf89usTkDx4zWibkudTySqN9C00b3K1v39rYVitquu8crnkVXtv32OsGm1ZTGmqRpKr5MrcoGjc9OwlXWEXJ6jzAODOEFG?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="316" width="602"></span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">My app nickname will be angularBlogApp. Let’s leave the ‘Also set up Firebase Hosting for this app’ unchecked. We’ll use App Hosting for fullstack SSR/SSG Angular apps. You can find the documentation here:</span><a href="https://firebase.google.com/docs/app-hosting?hl=en&amp;authuser=0" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://firebase.google.com/docs/app-hosting?hl=en&amp;authuser=0" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Firebase App Hosting</a></u><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">After registering the app we get out configuration:</span></div><div></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXc4JNS4lxnw419_U2Hnj-7IHkOwvO8GwWrXIc1WrHK6bVbfxQJ3aafoFWIyvNpawdO4Ne_63GAB8as52C6wJj3ML-jZsUaj23bJw5zQQ2T2bhkupR5kj7GJX4kVQjK-hQ4MObPoyot6D6eOThAPWgapHSQ?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="456" width="602"></span></div><div></div><div></div><h1 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">CREATE AN APP</span></h1><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Now we Can go to the next step and create Angular app with angular CLI</span></div><ul><li><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">ng new angularblogapp</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> (needs to be lowercase),</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">let’s use SCSS,</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Make sure to set </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Y</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> for “</span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Do you want to enable Server-Side Rendering (SSR) and Static Site Generation (SSG/Prerendering)? (y/N)</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">”,</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Now, we need to wait a little bit, then just </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">cd angularblogapp</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> and </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">code .</strong></li></ul><div></div><div class="ql-align-center"></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Let’s take a look at our files:</span></div><div></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdlfkXLxZNdhEFD238aQ0qfdkby_y1-QY6W8_s_ApcwADHiBUuMU7BZr4xEa_JCB5q0HCEMNanmmkIM6bKK_lff22RlC4j3oSwFO_usBkZi2n_dWUBFp9gt51LKxCwiWqeE7Kor2qXUUL2sfAYZy18QubE?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="745" width="356"></span></div><div></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">FILE STRUCTURE AND CONFIGURATION</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">In our project, we have a file called </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">server.ts</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">, which contains the configuration for our </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Express.js</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> server that serves prerendered app elements. You can find more information</span><a href="https://angular.dev/guide/ssr#example-1" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://angular.dev/guide/ssr#example-1" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a></u><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">We also have </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">main.server.ts,</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> where we bootstrap our configuration. We’ll need to add a bit of configuration at the start in </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">app.config.ts</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div></div><div></div><pre data-language="javascript"><code class="javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-attr">appConfig</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">ApplicationConfig</span> = { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">providers</span>: [ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideHttpClient</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">withFetch</span>()), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideZoneChangeDetection</span>({ <span class="hljs-attr">eventCoalescing</span>: <span class="hljs-literal">true</span> }), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideRouter</span>(routes), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideClientHydration</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">withEventReplay</span>()), &nbsp;] }; </code></pre><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Let’s add </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">provideHttpClient(withFetch())</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">. This provides the HttpClient to download data from the database to be prerendered. You can find more information</span><a href="https://angular.dev/guide/http/setup#configuring-features-of-httpclient" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://angular.dev/guide/http/setup#configuring-features-of-httpclient" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a></u><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Next, add </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">withEventReplay()</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> to the hydration config. This caches user requests before the app is fully hydrated. More details can be found</span><a href="https://angular.dev/api/platform-browser/withEventReplay#" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://angular.dev/api/platform-browser/withEventReplay#" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a></u><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Ok, now let’s go to </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">app.confg.server.ts</strong></div><pre data-language="javascript"><code class="javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-attr">serverConfig</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">ApplicationConfig</span> = { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">providers</span>: [ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideServerRendering</span>(), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideClientHydration</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">withEventReplay</span>()), &nbsp;] }; </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">We also need to add hydration on the server side. You can find more information</span><a href="https://angular.dev/errors/NG0505#debugging-the-error" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://angular.dev/errors/NG0505#debugging-the-error" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a></u><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Let’s move on to the next part. In your Angular app, run ng g environments and open </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">environment.development.ts</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">. Then, add our configuration.</span></div><pre data-language="javascript"><code class="javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> environment = { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">production</span>: <span class="hljs-literal">false</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">firebase</span>: { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">apiKey</span>: <span class="hljs-string">"***"</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">authDomain</span>: <span class="hljs-string">"***"</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">projectId</span>: <span class="hljs-string">"angular-blog-dfd85"</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">storageBucket</span>: <span class="hljs-string">"***"</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">messagingSenderId</span>: <span class="hljs-string">"***"</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">appId</span>: <span class="hljs-string">"***"</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">measurementId</span>: <span class="hljs-string">"***"</span> &nbsp;} }; </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Do the same in </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">environment.ts </strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">but remove production: false.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Next, install Firebase with </span></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">npm install firebase </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">If you are not logged in, you need to run firebase login.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">For the next part, go to the App console and run:</span></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">ng add @angular/fire </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">The package @angular/fire (in v18.0.1 current) will be installed and executed. Select “Y” to confirm.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">When asked, “What features would you like to set up?” choose:</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> • Authentication</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> • Firestore</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> • Cloud Functions (callable)</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> • Cloud Storage</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Then press Enter.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Choose your email address for Firebase (you might have multiple; there are tutorials online if needed).We will use the existing project - angularBlog, so choose it, and then select angularBlogApp from the apps. It will update our </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">app.config.ts</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">, but Firebase does this in a not very clean way.</span></div><pre data-language="javascript"><code class="javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-attr">appConfig</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">ApplicationConfig</span> = { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">providers</span>: [ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideHttpClient</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">withFetch</span>()), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideZoneChangeDetection</span>({ <span class="hljs-attr">eventCoalescing</span>: <span class="hljs-literal">true</span> }), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideRouter</span>(routes), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideClientHydration</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">withEventReplay</span>()), <span class="hljs-title function_">provideFirebaseApp</span>(<span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">initializeApp</span>({<span class="hljs-string">"projectId"</span>:<span class="hljs-string">"-267d7"</span>,<span class="hljs-string">"appId"</span>:<span class="hljs-string">"1:**:web:e9d17af5c6472c101684bc"</span>,<span class="hljs-string">"storageBucket"</span>:<span class="hljs-string">"angularblog-267d7.appspot.com"</span>,<span class="hljs-string">"apiKey"</span>:<span class="hljs-string">"AIzaSyAV55u4H2C0i8n0DUl5Ym_cJYjOl0NwQck"</span>,<span class="hljs-string">"authDomain"</span>:<span class="hljs-string">"angularblog-267d7.firebaseapp.com"</span>,<span class="hljs-string">"messagingSenderId"</span>:<span class="hljs-string">"247576047093"</span>,<span class="hljs-string">"measurementId"</span>:<span class="hljs-string">"G-QEE6VH1NP0"</span>})), <span class="hljs-title function_">provideAuth</span>(<span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">getAuth</span>()), <span class="hljs-title function_">provideFirestore</span>(<span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">getFirestore</span>()), <span class="hljs-title function_">provideFunctions</span>(<span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">getFunctions</span>()), <span class="hljs-title function_">provideStorage</span>(<span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">getStorage</span>())] }; </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">now looks much better</span></div><pre data-language="javascript"><code class="javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-attr">appConfig</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">ApplicationConfig</span> = { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">providers</span>: [ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideHttpClient</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">withFetch</span>()), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideZoneChangeDetection</span>({ <span class="hljs-attr">eventCoalescing</span>: <span class="hljs-literal">true</span> }), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideRouter</span>(routes), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideClientHydration</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">withEventReplay</span>()), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideFirebaseApp</span>(<span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">initializeApp</span>(environment.<span class="hljs-property">firebase</span>)), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideAuth</span>(<span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">getAuth</span>()), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideFirestore</span>(<span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">getFirestore</span>()), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideFunctions</span>(<span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">getFunctions</span>()), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">provideStorage</span>(<span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">getStorage</span>())] }; </code></pre><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">APP HOSTING SETUP</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">OK, next step. Go back to the Firebase Console, to the project overview, and from the left menu, select “</span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Build</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">” then “</span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">App Hosting</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">”.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Let’s initialize our project in VS Code with </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">git init</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">. I hope you are familiar with Git.</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcnzXFyvb2ubT5timJGnZfPXaauQ1LkV7GqiEOUqnor9mPq10BqhEKstFG851tPobvYvV2Iydv1gkTRDIJrGB5wNZvXu9vbpC08qqE5e8rNjGUALhoDiSNSORluRohOffmw6lLDqhiJ7ZuoEEAwgWxl8W1D?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="831" width="243"></span></div><div></div><div></div><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">You will see the screen below:</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfhnqrWHAgL9R-gDGrlfSkJUDYb7pQYRg27vT6_IzT2tGDEJZHVqqh8P48QGlTPo7dYHlVtQabQ9zk6UFCpq_ZJEhg7MeBYxaDivTFRY9hTysKXVAVpJxY4WY2fpmG7iT9rJj1Jfr6doD2hL_McOKetUdFr?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="289" width="602"></span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">We need to upgrade the project to </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Blaze</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> (Pay as you go). I have already created my billing account, so I will select it and click. If you don’t have an account, just click the “</span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Create a billing account</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">” button and add your card details.</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdFQMd8dfr6QPbewi52xyslYdazg85HOGqq7OCpLBv3BrBvl4GzuYUEVTWM6YfqFI-yp-z_qX4gEYPtXd7VSB3taUUsI5ObB3ChAjmh4OrBxeowAVtU10MqPH26bhDUQ9GQ9aJMr86GUSK1qFaHp5ZpvR7s?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="380" width="602"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">To make sure I don’t mess anything up, I set a budget to 10 PLN (which is about $2.50). Not much, but it ensures that during development I won’t get hit with a surprise bill. Plus, I’ll get an email when I reach 50%, 90%, and 100% of my budget. That’s pretty awesome, right?</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Now, just go to the next page, and if everything looks good (it does for me), click the “Purchase” button. Great, we’re done! BTW, we also need the Blaze plan to use Functions, but I’ll cover that later.</span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Everything is fine, so let’s get started. </span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXceyhKNREAIWQVuIlVA3riQiAc9CMpxAh10kG8z0UC8KtnCPJ-NofA78SdqhR25qmUC4JcrOVNbs37S12XKHbeq7odFH5mFUKPSLv0H6qHsNTdSgqSxNJv2YqaoEpGRFNAvTYDKYJ7jHEuU4uya0DpOIHo?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="229" width="409"></span></div><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Let’s connect with GitHub. It’s a simple OAuth process, so I’ll skip the details. Check the repo you created at the beginning of this tutorial. If you skipped that step, you can create it now, but note that it won’t update the dropdown automatically. You’ll need to start the setup of hosting once again.</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfLyuSUW_ydPo4Trpuixp6cHsO_EB5Jr9i7ZefFC1XnQoCiRFq6PJ3L5EWBLAOVVjRuhCdP3suz9y_A60eOOTe9iy6T5mjhkc-qLCEW_w2HkEDWLeGRVoLUwMg7JEvYA5d1o7ABHtpmkpOSnwhXPbyaCqxP?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="465" width="602"></span></div><div class="ql-align-center"></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">I will leave automatic rollouts to build the app in every push to the main.</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcZTsZ7TCMIndybH5Iyc0SBoDTz_r4KyFFYjY_kOdbF02KyW22eZfhepvcVEPlZP5NX_wFJY_tz5ZXHiOmSNTEAtdiZPbJDTWFKtmDT2ZSkjZXYIiJjj-Dyz4ZzuXY5qGhm3N9GM72dalfQONDBsEDChPU?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="311" width="602"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">My app name will be “</span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">blogbe</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">” and I want to manually select my app from the list.</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXeFOzYwABeZpl3wCgQB4f3ZkgRCmAf_kfZJl_GbkgvWgLAGEUXvFBo3rx7SXSyvPE30ObLvOdT-bmU47AaXTLsKU3rYdnyBQde8Cpygc6EaVFDvTKyxAe5rpF3uhrVyoLpyeAch1PWbKg6-npYM9tLFxoY?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="308" width="602"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> Finish and deploy</span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">We need to wait a minute… and success! We’ve done it!</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> </span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcaY74ilEr9yswwMEXmcVmGPYr7ZRMIraNspzD_zCwzwVEIXL-K5YALtufa2rq1mx9PoeZgC1mHgpDFxDZpjkNw7je5jOzRTuxNOZy8pg7c34sGxnYZ-LqXOyymq8I46TyVvpLky04098fTNfVhT8YxrB8?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="371" width="602"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">You can go to “</span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">View dashboard</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">”&nbsp;</span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Here you can see that the app is being built right now. Domains are listed, and there is a button labeled “</span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Create rollout</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">” to manually trigger the build.</span></div><div></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcHTvJ2oRtJREXIQf55ietAO-deEKHJFtc9yI3PwkAhQUb1kXshPRWuwBeu3sgYzo5Q3qmxbLf3iiKrGwSFDK-Y9x_cAZgTrlgCqcVrg9mbLbBF0yEM9TnWZgPIC4F6upeLU-71EMt38dWquXpUSww1ehE?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="289" width="602"></span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">This usually takes a bit of time, so go ahead and make yourself a coffee or tea. Even if the app has already been built, you might see some issues with the server, like “</span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">ERR_SSL_VERSION_OR_CIPHER_MISMATCH</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.” Just wait a few more minutes.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">After a few minutes, ta-dah! Our first small success: our app is displaying an Angular placeholder. 🎉</span></div><div></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcT7nsn1hzNe_de_QUPNt7oKdELgWZMM1mTB5pWVbUEJ_FdlfBXGB1JAwhhLIjBFaqM8xXKdv1MHogC-f55slkysQKYpVvIcv1AFFX_04BH8f3lxDszK-fFnknQP3RgUoc1kmPSt5UYLvuHJvn1t87Zr2Y?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="335" width="602"></span></div><div class="ql-align-center"></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">FE SIDE APP DEVELOPMENT</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Our application will have two parts:</span></div><ol><li><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Blog application: Mostly SSG.</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Administrator console: Lazy-loaded, a standard Angular app without prerendering.</span></li></ol><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">So let’s dive straight into our code.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">First, let’s get rid of the Angular placeholders. In app.component.html, we will have only:</span></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">router-outlet</span>&gt;</span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">router-outlet</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Now, let’s create the Reader Component, which will be a wrapper for the blog reader side:</span></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">ng g c Reader </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">And similarly for the admin:</span></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">ng g c Admin </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Oh, I forgot to pass the --</span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">onPush</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> flag! Let’s change that now and add </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">RouterOutlet</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> in the imports for both components.</span></div><div></div><div></div><pre data-language="javascript"><code class="javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { <span class="hljs-title class_">ChangeDetectionStrategy</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">Component</span> } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''@angular/core''</span>; <span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { <span class="hljs-title class_">RouterOutlet</span> } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''@angular/router''</span>; <span class="hljs-meta">@Component</span>({ &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">selector</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''app-reader''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">standalone</span>: <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">imports</span>: [<span class="hljs-title class_">RouterOutlet</span>], &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">templateUrl</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''./reader.component.html''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">styleUrl</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''./reader.component.scss''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">changeDetection</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">ChangeDetectionStrategy</span>.<span class="hljs-property">OnPush</span> }) <span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">ReaderComponent</span> { } </code></pre><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">OK, now we have some starters here. Let’s add a new folder called </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">shared</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> and inside it, another folder called </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">_models</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">In the </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">_models</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> folder, we’ll create our models for the app, which will be used with Firestore to create our collections in the database.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Let’s start with the minimum number of models. We definitely need interfaces for:</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> • Blog</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> • Comments</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">For the user, we’ll use the Firebase user entity.</span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">OK, so our Blog interface will look like this:</span></div><pre data-language="javascript"><code class="javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">interface</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">Blog</span> { &nbsp;id?: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">title</span>: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">content</span>: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;description?: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;author?: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;date?: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;image?: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;tags?: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>[]; &nbsp;likes?: <span class="hljs-built_in">number</span>; &nbsp;comments?: <span class="hljs-title class_">Comment</span>[]; &nbsp;shares?: <span class="hljs-built_in">number</span>; &nbsp;views?: <span class="hljs-built_in">number</span>; &nbsp;status?: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;category?: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;commentsEnabled?: <span class="hljs-built_in">boolean</span>; &nbsp;likesEnabled?: <span class="hljs-built_in">boolean</span>; } </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">It’s quite big, but Copilot helped me with that. I just selected the hints it gave me. Now, let’s move on to the Comment interface.</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">interface</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">Comment</span> { &nbsp;id?: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">content</span>: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;author?: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;date?: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;likes?: <span class="hljs-built_in">number</span>; &nbsp;replies?: <span class="hljs-title class_">Comment</span>[]; &nbsp;status?: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;likesEnabled?: <span class="hljs-built_in">boolean</span>; &nbsp;repliesEnabled?: <span class="hljs-built_in">boolean</span>; } </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">I’m very happy with what Copilot proposed to me, so I accepted all of its suggestions.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">OK, let’s jump to our </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">app.routes.ts</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> and add our routes. The Admin section isn’t needed at the start, so let’s lazy-load it.</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-attr">routes</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">Routes</span> = [ &nbsp;{ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">path</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''''</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">children</span>: readerRoutes, &nbsp;}, &nbsp;{ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">path</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''admin''</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">loadChildren</span>: <span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">import</span>(<span class="hljs-string">''./admin/admin.routes''</span>).<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function"><span class="hljs-params">r</span> =&gt;</span> r.<span class="hljs-property">adminRoutes</span>), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">title</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''Admin''</span>, &nbsp;}, ]; </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">We need some data, so jump into the admin folder, create a subfolder called _components, and create a component for creating blog posts with:</span></div><pre data-language="plaintext"><code class="plaintext">ng g c -c OnPush AddPost </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">For now, we’ll just use simple inputs, then we’ll add PrimeNG and use their editor later (check it out</span><a href="https://primeng.org/editor" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://primeng.org/editor" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a></u><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">). But we’ll save that for later. Our blog needs only two properties, so let’s create a simple form for now. We’ll polish it later. I’ll use ChatGPT (the new versions work great with Angular docs) to quickly create a prototype.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Now, in our </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">add-post-component.html</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">, we can start building your form.</span></div><div></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">form</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">formGroup</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"blogForm"</span> (<span class="hljs-attr">ngSubmit</span>)=<span class="hljs-string">"onSubmit()"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">label</span> <span class="hljs-attr">for</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"title"</span>&gt;</span>Title:<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">label</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">input</span> <span class="hljs-attr">id</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"title"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">formControlName</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"title"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">required</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;@if (blogForm.get(''title'')?.invalid &amp;&amp; (blogForm.get(''title'')?.dirty || blogForm.get(''title'')?.touched)) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;@if (blogForm.get(''title'')?.errors?.[''required'']) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span>Title is required.<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;} &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">label</span> <span class="hljs-attr">for</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"content"</span>&gt;</span>Content:<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">label</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">input</span> <span class="hljs-attr">id</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"content"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">formControlName</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"content"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">required</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;@if (blogForm.get(''content'')?.invalid &amp;&amp; (blogForm.get(''content'')?.dirty || blogForm.get(''content'')?.touched)) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;@if (blogForm.get(''content'')?.errors?.[''required'']) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span>Content is required.<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;} &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">button</span> <span class="hljs-attr">type</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"submit"</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">disabled</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"blogForm.invalid"</span>&gt;</span>Submit<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">button</span>&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">form</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><div></div><div><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">add-post-component.ts</strong></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-meta">@Component</span>({ &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">selector</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''app-add-post''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">standalone</span>: <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>, <span class="hljs-attr">imports</span>: [<span class="hljs-title class_">ReactiveFormsModule</span>], &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">templateUrl</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''./add-post.component.html''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">styleUrl</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''./add-post.component.scss''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">changeDetection</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">ChangeDetectionStrategy</span>.<span class="hljs-property">OnPush</span> }) <span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">AddPostComponent</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">blogForm</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">FormGroup</span>; &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">private</span> fb = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">FormBuilder</span>); &nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">constructor</span>(<span class="hljs-params"></span>) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">blogForm</span> = <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">fb</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">group</span>({ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">title</span>: [<span class="hljs-string">''''</span>, [<span class="hljs-title class_">Validators</span>.<span class="hljs-property">required</span>]], &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">content</span>: [<span class="hljs-string">''''</span>, [<span class="hljs-title class_">Validators</span>.<span class="hljs-property">required</span>]] &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}); &nbsp;} &nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">onSubmit</span>(): <span class="hljs-built_in">void</span> { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">blogForm</span>.<span class="hljs-property">valid</span>) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable language_">console</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">log</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">blogForm</span>.<span class="hljs-property">value</span>); &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;} } </code></pre><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">SENDING DATA TO FIRESTORE</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Let’s create a new folder called _services in the admin folder. Inside this folder, we’ll create an API service.&nbsp;</span></div><pre data-language="plaintext"><code class="plaintext">ng g s Api - could be AdminApi </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Erase </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">providedIn: ''root''</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> because we don’t want a singleton; we want a lazy-loaded service for a super smooth and fast reader side.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Our service is quite simple for now.</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-meta">@Injectable</span>() <span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">ApiService</span> { &nbsp;firestore = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">Firestore</span>); &nbsp;http = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">HttpClient</span>); &nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">addBlog</span>(<span class="hljs-params"><span class="hljs-attr">blog</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">Blog</span></span>) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> newTaskRef = <span class="hljs-title function_">doc</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">collection</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">firestore</span>, <span class="hljs-string">''blog''</span>)); &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">setDoc</span>(newTaskRef, blog); &nbsp;} } </code></pre><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">and in </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">add-post.component.ts</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> we update onSubmit() Method</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-title function_">onSubmit</span>(): <span class="hljs-built_in">void</span> { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">blogForm</span>.<span class="hljs-property">valid</span>) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">apiService</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">addBlog</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">blogForm</span>.<span class="hljs-property">value</span>); &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;} } </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">and providers and imports</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-meta">@Component</span>({ &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">selector</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''blog-add-post''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">standalone</span>: <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">imports</span>: [<span class="hljs-title class_">ReactiveFormsModule</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">FirestoreModule</span>], &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">providers</span>: [<span class="hljs-title class_">ApiService</span>], &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">templateUrl</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''./add-post.component.html''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">styleUrl</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''./add-post.component.scss''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">changeDetection</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">ChangeDetectionStrategy</span>.<span class="hljs-property">OnPush</span> }) </code></pre><h2 class="ql-align-center"></h2><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">LITTLE BREAK</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Meanwhile, I tried to run my app and caught a strange error:</span></div><div><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">main.ts:5 ERROR TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading ''_ejsa'')</strong></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">This error is caused by </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">withEventReplay()</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> in </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">app.config.ts</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">. From what I see on Google, it’s a common issue. Check out</span><a href="https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/56122" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/56122" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">this GitHub issue</a></u><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> for more details. It’s already fixed, but the fix hasn’t been released yet, so we’ll have to wait and come back to it later.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Another error I encountered is:</span></div><div><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">ERROR RuntimeError: NG0204: Can''t resolve all parameters for Firestore2: (?).</strong></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Strange error caused by</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { <span class="hljs-title class_">Firestore</span> } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''firebase/firestore''</span>; </code></pre><div>lets change to</div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { <span class="hljs-title class_">Firestore</span>} <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''@angular/fire/firestore''</span>; </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Working now.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Next, go back to the Firebase Console to configure Firestore.</span></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">FIRESTORE SETUP</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Go to the</span><a href="https://console.firebase.google.com/project/angularblog-267d7/firestore" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://console.firebase.google.com/project/angularblog-267d7/firestore" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Firebase Console</a></u><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">. Just like with App Hosting, on the left side, click the “</span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Build</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">” dropdown and select “</span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Firestore Database</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.”</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdk9FVM84FePWOFDG7P-fqWhdinuS2WjxsaMScAljajAK0jbvAM0868pE6islJCM0J_4tQr9tFhRduQTCs2mj2GgDblRVDHms9yWSU5OFq_ThahGLfLUcNl1DAchc-Zb-3iRvOjwwxdiT_eAFboWQ_fZssB?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="692" width="249"></span></div><div class="ql-align-center"></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">and “</span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Create database</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">”</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXe32arWLP31K299oqMZeVsw9PzWyMJqYyM_F7AALbnXX6SLjKevhor0G3W5etmTM1poutf2E2Rc87GzSIXdh6Gf0kbWt9qeOf2RJGDCIatGFMGTbapiZ2ARt3wPalLftOXjQK6o-XWW5r2-Y9fVf0EJ5fk?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="357" width="438"></span></div><div class="ql-align-center"></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Set DatabaseID and Location, click “</span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Next</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">”</span></div><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">We’ll start in </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">test mode</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> because we haven’t set up the authentication yet. That means anyone with a reference can manipulate the data, which is why I set a $3 limit.</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdMWBTreXCyzA28vU9wlkQTHXnOSNxHZCyJ3bsW5ufa2SU1J74eHdp_hJhv8S6lUPhrsJd6toIx7FruCK5dc-JGTuqZMDl5gmWoTbe3fqmOjX4aMTXIFUvJA73eoSBIPVaOd-q6BofVy6ACii1-3ik7XJQr?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="416" width="602"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Click “</span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Create</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">”, it will take a while.&nbsp;</span></div><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Now let''s go to the </span><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="http://localhost:4200/admin" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">admin page</a></u><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXeawWFtGl4ULnghpp6TNIIlC41cJjdSByYKQ4ofURcxRBh9FoE5oikjVvOYvwNfYYGHHl2sprA4IRm5ykam_KVXjPx-r9kAsnM7yO5akW5l9akjD2hMpOOW8AVFiGXJYDDlVR29A6YFq2Thf0dVHYHLUhHM?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="68" width="510"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">I tried to submit the form, but nothing happened. I connected to my other project’s database, and everything worked fine, so let’s take a look at the config. Everything looks fine to me. I dropped the database and recreated it, but now my database name is “(</span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">default</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">)”. I also created it in prod mode and manually changed the rules to:</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdtY0mQFk-5uGZydgafS2UYDGr0jiicl2cvwbV4RqD6T1fLPoYW5LmM0Qte1uNprW06Vgci6IqwJSxk5m18nxfdo6IRr40XmiE-onT4iqxGRtVHN8um6MHLMJv_nbs2EqNdQp2hTQEPBMMg9BqyUYe-uoA?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="309" width="602"></span></div><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">as we can see there is data in DB!</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXeKteZ-h5aSH2D69Omr75vBuxjFM_mADCiuMb4qfa2d5n7lQBBLnSchJtv9rXvS3J-h7MpwEQeD0Bt29wCme76cEiN9OucYLpdKTK4b55FFjnsPptQtHkyCHVcHS4jcwTf58Z970C9oUyJjpvKf-M4h5oQ?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="195" width="602"></span></div><div></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">BUILDING APP LOCALLY</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">We can now do </span></div><pre data-language="plaintext"><code class="plaintext">ng build </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">and go to the </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">dist</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> folder.&nbsp;</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXd9j1ak_TWhDounbzcSrkREaeZVA_N12LT6LEr7uM_jNVqYGr-i006SKvBf_Nv0plbnHxiFf6HzZyt6US0wZRg9t-ixjWHNoli01ECQn-yXg0N2yvMAT6YtOhmOsxPp7dDdspTW6L78EdwDCzDCzcokypM?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="670" width="566"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Let’s take a look at </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">admin/index.html</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">. Oops! It seems that even though Admin is lazy-loaded, it’s still pre rendered. 🙁 Well, that wasn’t part of the plan!</span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcurY2S_sQFP-jImNjZG_FkkJTt-aRcOiuf9lJFW2TmVLRXozSqsxQQ7qHYVPMW9o7TUmDvQQqIMuftM-8RtSSxzkF_nZFiAVjoIvpSfA1FMCErbWUSEBRb0bAyH0m1O8hNchz-Tbt8IIF_tmxw77qxuroH?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="172" width="602"></span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">But that is OK! Just wrap everything in </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">add-post.component.html </strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">with:</span></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml">@defer {} </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Rebuild. </span><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Problem solved! 🎉</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfY4Jtp-ZBbAnH_OkCpqQaTdpSeP--_pgr_bjCCgPLDhIqPVZir5qYfC__94GHlihYGqhPsMW0pOBxQ9vaOTq5N_9l91u16ryjgUIJIbkNymSs_wOWaPOrJU3fMjNltIX-htaoiURHNeg4qbTHYmIvjgqDS?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="192" width="602"></span></div><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Well, there’s no submit button, so the Admin HTML isn’t prerendered. We can use this for some larger components with JS that they use. Check out</span><a href="https://angular.dev/api/core/@defer" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://angular.dev/api/core/@defer" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">@defer</a></u><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">We can also create a component wrapper to defer the whole </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">add-blog-post component</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.&nbsp;</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">I think I’ll use that later for another purpose. Imagine in the future our blog has 100 posts, each with images. That’s quite a lot of data. Can we not prerender it? Yes, but we still want SEO optimization for our blog.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">The </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">@defer</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> decorator has great options like </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">@placeholder</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> or </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">@loading</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">. So, instead of prerendering the entire blog post, we can just prerender a tag and maybe a summary. This will definitely make the load time a lot faster for the client.</span></div><div></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">FETCH DATA FROM FIRESTORE</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Now that we’ve got some data, let’s switch back to the Reader side. Let’s generate the main component:</span></div><pre data-language="plaintext"><code class="plaintext">ng g c -c OnPush MainPage&nbsp; </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">and _services folder with API service inside&nbsp;</span></div><pre data-language="plaintext"><code class="plaintext">ng g s ReaderApi </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">let’s add some logic to service.</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-meta">@Injectable</span>() <span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">ApiServiceService</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">private</span> firestore = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">Firestore</span>); &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">private</span> collection = <span class="hljs-title function_">collection</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">firestore</span>, <span class="hljs-string">''blog''</span>); &nbsp;blog$ = <span class="hljs-title function_">collectionData</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">collection</span>, {<span class="hljs-attr">idField</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''id''</span>}) <span class="hljs-keyword">as</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">Observable</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-title class_">Blog</span>[]&gt;; } </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Not that much to do, and we have a strongly typed observable that will trigger when the data is updated. Let’s add some data visualization in the HTML.</span></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"container"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"row"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;@for (item of blog$ | async; track item.id) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span>{{ item.title}}<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span>{{item.content}}<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">That was quite easy, and now we have our blog list! Later, we’ll wrap it into a card, but let’s leave the CSS stuff for the part near the end.</span></div><div></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"container"</span>&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"container"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"row"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;@for (item of blog$ | async; track item.id) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">a</span>&nbsp;[<span class="hljs-attr">routerLink</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"[''/post'', item.id]"</span> &gt;</span>{{ item.title}}<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">a</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span>{{item.content}}<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><div></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">CREATE MAIN PAGE, POST AND COMMENTS COMPONENTS</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">OK, let’s create a specific blog post component.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">First of all, let’s add the </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">withComponentInputBinding() </strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">statement in app.config.ts, so we can catch the ID with </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">@Input()</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">. For more details, check out</span><a href="https://angular.dev/guide/routing/routing-with-urlmatcher#configure-your-routes-for-your-application" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://angular.dev/guide/routing/routing-with-urlmatcher#configure-your-routes-for-your-application" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">this guide</a></u><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Now, create a post component in </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">src/app/reader/_components/main-page</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">:</span></div><pre data-language="plaintext"><code class="plaintext">ng g c -c OnPush Post </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">And update </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">reader.routes.ts</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> accordingly.</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-attr">readerRoutes</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">Routes</span> = [ &nbsp;{ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">path</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''''</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">component</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">MainPageComponent</span>, &nbsp;}, &nbsp;{ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">path</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''post/:id''</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">component</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">PostComponent</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">pathMatch</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''full''</span> &nbsp;} ]; </code></pre><div></div><div>We can check and console log id:</div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">PostComponent</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">implements</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">OnInit</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-meta">@Input</span>() id!: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">ngOnInit</span>(<span class="hljs-params"></span>) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable language_">console</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">log</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">id</span>); &nbsp;} } </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Let’s click on the post link.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdRpnD3U8Zf76jztO47HGUwvdFkZd8HNTNb3ru4xVDmTQ6NsX34lqMBWMwE-YdsIi7GUgevtHc8pVu-pOT35cBYG8WNv75Y7jEIhi9wZebP2waK4vw900Y8GduWhlhMc23h69Kck7s-r6Fgyx5Ioo1uDR7m?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="19" width="393"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Everything is working as expected!.</span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Now, let’s create a getPost method to fetch a specific blog post.</span></div><div></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript">&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">private</span> firestore = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">Firestore</span>); &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">private</span> collection = <span class="hljs-title function_">collection</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">firestore</span>, <span class="hljs-string">''blog''</span>); &nbsp;blog$ = <span class="hljs-title function_">collectionData</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">collection</span>, {<span class="hljs-attr">idField</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''id''</span>}) <span class="hljs-keyword">as</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">Observable</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-title class_">Blog</span>[]&gt;; &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">async</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">getPost</span>(<span class="hljs-attr">id</span>: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>): <span class="hljs-title class_">Promise</span>&lt; <span class="hljs-title class_">Blog</span> | <span class="hljs-literal">null</span>&gt; { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">getDoc</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">doc</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">collection</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">firestore</span>, <span class="hljs-string">''blog''</span>), id)).<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">doc</span>) =&gt;</span> { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (doc.<span class="hljs-title function_">exists</span>()) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> doc.<span class="hljs-title function_">data</span>() <span class="hljs-keyword">as</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">Blog</span>; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} <span class="hljs-keyword">else</span> { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class="hljs-literal">null</span>; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}); &nbsp;} </code></pre><div></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">PostComponent</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">implements</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">OnInit</span>{ &nbsp;<span class="hljs-meta">@Input</span>() id!: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;apiService = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">ReaderApiService</span>); &nbsp;post$!: <span class="hljs-title class_">Observable</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-title class_">Blog</span> | <span class="hljs-literal">null</span>&gt;; &nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">ngOnInit</span>(<span class="hljs-params"></span>) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">post$</span> = <span class="hljs-title function_">from</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">apiService</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">getPost</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">id</span>)); &nbsp;} } </code></pre><div></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;{{post$ | async | json}} <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Of course, under a post, we want to have comments. So let’s create two components: </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">AddComment</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> and </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Comments</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><pre data-language="plaintext"><code class="plaintext">ng g c -c OnPush AddComment ng g c -c OnPush Comments </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">OK, let’s create some API calls in </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">ReaderApiService</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-title function_">getComments</span>(<span class="hljs-params"><span class="hljs-attr">postId</span>: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span></span>) { <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">collectionData</span>( <span class="hljs-title function_">collection</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">firestore</span>, <span class="hljs-string">`<span class="hljs-subst">${Collections.POST}</span>/<span class="hljs-subst">${postId}</span>/<span class="hljs-subst">${Collections.COMMENT}</span>`</span>), {<span class="hljs-attr">idField</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''id''</span>}) <span class="hljs-keyword">as</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">Observable</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-title class_">Comment</span>[]&gt;; } <span class="hljs-title function_">addComment</span>(<span class="hljs-params"><span class="hljs-attr">postId</span>: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>, <span class="hljs-attr">comment</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">Comment</span></span>) { <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> newTaskRef = <span class="hljs-title function_">doc</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">collection</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">firestore</span>, <span class="hljs-string">`<span class="hljs-subst">${Collections.POST}</span>/<span class="hljs-subst">${postId}</span>/<span class="hljs-subst">${Collections.COMMENT}</span>`</span>)); <span class="hljs-title function_">setDoc</span>(newTaskRef, comment).<span class="hljs-title function_">finally</span>(<span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-variable language_">console</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">log</span>(<span class="hljs-string">''comment added ''</span>, newTaskRef.<span class="hljs-property">id</span>); }); } </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">For now we can re-use the form generated by GPT for comment too.</span></div><div><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">add-comment.component.html</strong></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">form</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">formGroup</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"commentForm"</span> (<span class="hljs-attr">ngSubmit</span>)=<span class="hljs-string">"onSubmit()"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">label</span> <span class="hljs-attr">for</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"content"</span>&gt;</span>Content:<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">label</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">input</span> <span class="hljs-attr">id</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"content"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">formControlName</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"content"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">required</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;@if (commentForm.get(''content'')?.invalid &amp;&amp; (commentForm.get(''content'')?.dirty || &nbsp;commentForm.get(''content'')?.touched)) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;@if (commentForm.get(''content'')?.errors?.[''required'']) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span>Content is required.<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;} &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">button</span> <span class="hljs-attr">type</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"submit"</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">disabled</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"commentForm.invalid"</span>&gt;</span>Submit<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">button</span>&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">form</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">and typescript file</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-meta">@Input</span>() postId!: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">commentForm</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">FormGroup</span>; &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">private</span> fb = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">FormBuilder</span>); &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">private</span> apiService = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">ReaderApiService</span>); &nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">constructor</span>(<span class="hljs-params"></span>) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">commentForm</span> = <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">fb</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">group</span>({ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">content</span>: [<span class="hljs-string">''''</span>, [<span class="hljs-title class_">Validators</span>.<span class="hljs-property">required</span>]], &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}); &nbsp;} &nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">onSubmit</span>(): <span class="hljs-built_in">void</span> { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">commentForm</span>.<span class="hljs-property">valid</span>) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">apiService</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">addComment</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">postId</span>, <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">commentForm</span>.<span class="hljs-property">value</span>); &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;} </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">OK, now let’s display the comments. The Comments component will be a kind of dumb component, so we’ll use a new observable input for that. It’s not good to mix business logic with presentational components, but here we are not basing and reusable components</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Let’s convert the comments observable into a signal. We need to do this in ngOnInit because we need to wait for the ID input.</span></div><div></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">PostComponent</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">implements</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">OnInit</span>{ &nbsp;<span class="hljs-meta">@Input</span>() id!: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>; &nbsp;apiService = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">ReaderApiService</span>); &nbsp;injector = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">Injector</span>); &nbsp;post$!: <span class="hljs-title class_">Observable</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-title class_">Blog</span> | <span class="hljs-literal">null</span>&gt;; &nbsp;comments$!: <span class="hljs-title class_">Signal</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-title class_">Comment</span>[] | <span class="hljs-literal">undefined</span>&gt;; &nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">ngOnInit</span>(<span class="hljs-params"></span>) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">post$</span> = <span class="hljs-title function_">from</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">apiService</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">getPost</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">id</span>)); &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">comments$</span> = <span class="hljs-title function_">runInInjectionContext</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">injector</span>, <span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">toSignal</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">apiService</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">getComments</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">id</span>))); &nbsp;} } </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">and just pass it like input&nbsp;</span></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">comments</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">comments</span>$]=<span class="hljs-string">"comments$()"</span> &gt;</span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">comments</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">in </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">PostComponent:</strong></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">CommentsComponent</span>&nbsp;{ &nbsp;comments$ = input&lt;<span class="hljs-title class_">Comment</span>[] | <span class="hljs-literal">undefined</span>&gt;(); } {{ <span class="hljs-title function_">comments$</span>() | json}} </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Let see how it’s works:</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfXYZVCWI4f8qiADoXj_S3ylbfHaQ6se-aJ9sUVWQgXNhFDf2fMogeJPDoxqxdCVKcb68uuH1HqluucUzUqkCkWy1KfK_kdzqM00jzAvoHMl_n6E66L9N_OwkMzXhTCDgQRUvocQlJTx1454BBXCl9j4RbE?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="345" width="602"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">As we can see, Firestore maintains everything under the hood. collectionData() returns an Observable, so we don’t need to worry about subscribing to posts and handling updates manually. Plus, we can be sure that changes are propagated to all clients, ensuring everyone has the freshest data. How cool is that?</span></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">LETS STOP AND MAKE SOME IMPROVEMENTS AND FIXES</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">This is my first big project with Firebase; I’ve only done small tutorials before. So, let’s take a moment to reflect and make some improvements. First of all, I created a Blog model, but it’s not really a blog by itself. A better name would be Post, so let’s refactor that.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Another thing to address is those magic strings:</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-title function_">collection</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">firestore</span>, <span class="hljs-string">`blog/<span class="hljs-subst">${postId}</span>/comment`</span>), {<span class="hljs-attr">idField</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''id''</span>}) <span class="hljs-keyword">as</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">Observable</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-title class_">Comment</span>[]&gt;; </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">If I want to rename the Collection to Post from Blog, I need to rename it everywhere. What a nightmare! This was a big mistake at the beginning of the project. But let’s refactor it now.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Let’s add a new folder called _enums in the shared folder:</span></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">ng g enum collections </code></pre><div></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">enum</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">Collections</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable constant_">POST</span> = <span class="hljs-string">''post''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable constant_">COMMENT</span> = <span class="hljs-string">''comment''</span>, } </code></pre><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">As we can see</span><a href="https://firebase.google.com/docs/firestore/query-data/queries?hl=en&amp;authuser=0#query_operators" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://firebase.google.com/docs/firestore/query-data/queries?hl=en&amp;authuser=0#query_operators" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a></u><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">, Firebase uses string characters for query operators, like this:</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> q = <span class="hljs-title function_">query</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">collection</span>(db, <span class="hljs-string">"cities"</span>), <span class="hljs-title function_">where</span>(<span class="hljs-string">"capital"</span>, <span class="hljs-string">"=="</span>, <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>)); </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">So, we can also create an enum for operators:</span></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">ng g enum queryOperators </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">I asked ChatGPT to create these operators for me, and they look fine.</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">enum</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">QueryOperators</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable constant_">LESS_THAN</span> = <span class="hljs-string">''&lt;''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable constant_">LESS_THAN_OR_EQUAL</span> = <span class="hljs-string">''&lt;=''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable constant_">EQUAL</span> = <span class="hljs-string">''==''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable constant_">GREATER_THAN</span> = <span class="hljs-string">''&gt;''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable constant_">GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL</span> = <span class="hljs-string">''&gt;=''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable constant_">NOT_EQUAL</span> = <span class="hljs-string">''!=''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable constant_">ARRAY_CONTAINS</span> = <span class="hljs-string">''array-contains''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable constant_">ARRAY_CONTAINS_ANY</span> = <span class="hljs-string">''array-contains-any''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable constant_">IN</span> = <span class="hljs-string">''in''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable constant_">NOT_IN</span> = <span class="hljs-string">''not-in''</span> } </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Now it looks a lot better:</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> newTaskRef = <span class="hljs-title function_">doc</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">collection</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">firestore</span>, <span class="hljs-string">`<span class="hljs-subst">${Collections.COMMENT}</span>/<span class="hljs-subst">${postId}</span>/<span class="hljs-subst">${Collections.COMMENT}</span>`</span>)); </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Meanwhile I encountered a strange issue with hydration. It said that hydration failed and some components hadn’t been rendered properly within 30 seconds. But this issue disappeared after I made some code changes and then reverted to a previous version. Quite strange, but let’s move forward.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">I should mention that I had issues with rendering the admin side, with timeouts, or the reader site rendering in the admin subfolder. To fix the rendering issue with reader stuff in admin, I just added a specified route to posts.</span></div><div></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-attr">routes</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">Routes</span> = [ &nbsp;{ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">path</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''posts''</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">children</span>: readerRoutes, &nbsp;}, &nbsp;{ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">path</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''admin''</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">loadChildren</span>: <span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">import</span>(<span class="hljs-string">''./admin/admin.routes''</span>).<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function"><span class="hljs-params">r</span> =&gt;</span> r.<span class="hljs-property">adminRoutes</span>), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">title</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''Admin''</span>, &nbsp;}, ]; </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Take a look in the dist folder. In </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">posts/index.html,</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> you can see that…</span></div><div></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">_ngcontent-ng-c2232596419</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"container"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">_ngcontent-ng-c2232596419</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"row"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">a</span> <span class="hljs-attr">_ngcontent-ng-c2232596419</span> <span class="hljs-attr">href</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"/posts/post/2lkZK8w4QWvjEIsduqrh"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">jsaction</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"click:"</span>&gt;</span>New blog2<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">a</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span> <span class="hljs-attr">_ngcontent-ng-c2232596419</span>&gt;</span>New blog2<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">a</span> <span class="hljs-attr">_ngcontent-ng-c2232596419</span> <span class="hljs-attr">href</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"/posts/post/K7rmxulzoenCKJxoJOQc"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">jsaction</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"click:"</span>&gt;</span>New blog3<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">a</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span> <span class="hljs-attr">_ngcontent-ng-c2232596419</span>&gt;</span>New blog3<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">a</span> <span class="hljs-attr">_ngcontent-ng-c2232596419</span> <span class="hljs-attr">href</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"/posts/post/fOwXkEXeGhPvjmKrJoCD"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">jsaction</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"click:"</span>&gt;</span>New blog1<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">a</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span> <span class="hljs-attr">_ngcontent-ng-c2232596419</span>&gt;</span>New blog1<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-comment">&lt;!----&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><h2 class="ql-align-center"></h2><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">SETTING UP SSG ROUTES</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">It looks like only the </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">MainPageComponent</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> has been rendered. We also want to prerender the components inside. Let’s take a look at the documentation</span><a href="https://angular.dev/guide/prerendering#prerendering-parameterized-routes" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://angular.dev/guide/prerendering#prerendering-parameterized-routes" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a></u><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">To change the routes, add this to </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">routes.txt</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">:</span></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml">/posts/ /posts/post/2lkZK8w4QWvjEIsduqrh </code></pre><div></div><div><strong>Angular.json</strong>:</div><pre data-language="plaintext"><code class="plaintext">"prerender": { "routesFile": "routes.txt" }, "ssr": { "entry": "server.ts" } </code></pre><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXflfTwB7CGhDcyFt7I4eU7jcINL_rCB9KRfwKQ19mP3FMPEcuDy--_zbhVPKLmOVaru_czX8lp6R8LXKrE0Om3pxgsWzESQwvXAqQ3ueqUfrnd_f_3Hoi2_jjx_OrT1e9KQBQb9LGitC2zXHUxUckAeZqgK?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="401" width="602"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Nice! But how are we supposed to know the IDs? It’s pretty lame to put them in manually. I need to brainstorm a solution for that. But for now, let’s rearrange the code. We’re on live, so sorry for the mess!</span></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">FIXING ROUTING IN READER AND ADDING POSTLIST COMPONENT</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Go to </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">/src/app/reader/_components/main-page</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> and</span></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">ng g c -c OnPush PostsList </code></pre><div><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">MainPageComponent</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> will only contains&nbsp;</span></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml">&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">router-outlet</span>/&gt;</span> </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">inside HTML</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-meta">@Component</span>({ &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">selector</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''app-main-page''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">standalone</span>: <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">imports</span>: [<span class="hljs-title class_">RouterModule</span>], &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">templateUrl</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''./main-page.component.html''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">styleUrl</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''./main-page.component.scss''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">changeDetection</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">ChangeDetectionStrategy</span>.<span class="hljs-property">OnPush</span> }) <span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">MainPageComponent</span> {} </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">inside TS</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">and </span><strong style="background-color: transparent;">PostsListComponent</strong></div><div></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-meta">@Component</span>({ &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">selector</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''app-posts-list''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">standalone</span>: <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">imports</span>: [<span class="hljs-title class_">FirestoreModule</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">AsyncPipe</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">RouterLink</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">PostComponent</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">RouterModule</span>], &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">providers</span>: [<span class="hljs-title class_">ReaderApiService</span>], &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">templateUrl</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''./posts-list.component.html''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">styleUrl</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''./posts-list.component.scss''</span>, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">changeDetection</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">ChangeDetectionStrategy</span>.<span class="hljs-property">OnPush</span> }) <span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">PostsListComponent</span> { &nbsp;apiService = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">ReaderApiService</span>); &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">posts$</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">Observable</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-title class_">Post</span>[]&gt; = <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">apiService</span>.<span class="hljs-property">posts$</span>; } </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">and HTML</span></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"container"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"row"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;@for (item of posts$ | async; track item.id) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">a</span>&nbsp;[<span class="hljs-attr">routerLink</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"[''post'',item.id]"</span> &gt;</span>{{ item.title}}<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">a</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span>{{item.content}}<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Again I’m getting timeouts issue</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXf8cFMm0SaYjeA0LwF2vZtQo0VdXO8Of4tkxqGOPEp7utkmyKe0JHgOgwm01NLyRZgkd_HiE-whc4wRI0S396B8LPgazG5brpp-L4jgFgyUW7iJ1jxSJe6nNPGQoTx0cLh_9PaPxgVCulv9O2eHonqWEEe5?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="353" width="594"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">and&nbsp;</span></div><pre data-language="plaintext"><code class="plaintext">main.ts:5 NG0506: Angular hydration expected the ApplicationRef.isStable() to emit `true`, but it didn''t happen within 10000ms. Angular hydration logic depends on the application becoming stable as a signal to complete hydration process. Find more at docs </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Issue comes from:</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">async</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">getPost</span>(<span class="hljs-attr">id</span>: <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>): <span class="hljs-title class_">Promise</span>&lt; <span class="hljs-title class_">Post</span> | <span class="hljs-literal">null</span>&gt; { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">getDoc</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">doc</span>(<span class="hljs-title function_">collection</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">firestore</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">Collections</span>.<span class="hljs-property">POST</span>), id)).<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">doc</span>) =&gt;</span> { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (doc.<span class="hljs-title function_">exists</span>()) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> doc.<span class="hljs-title function_">data</span>() <span class="hljs-keyword">as</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">Post</span>; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} <span class="hljs-keyword">else</span> { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class="hljs-literal">null</span>; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}); &nbsp;} </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Let’s try to figure this out.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">After 1 hour of investigating, the issue has been found!</span></div><div></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { getDoc } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''firebase/firestore''</span>; </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(106, 153, 85); background-color: transparent;">instead of</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { collectionData, doc, setDoc, getDoc } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''@angular/fire/firestore''</span>; </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">I think I need to write this on my hand: “</span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"><u>If you have issues with fetching from Firestore, first check your imports.</u></strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">”</span></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">PUSH TO THE REMOTE AND CHECK PROGRESS</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">OK, let’s push the changes and take a look at the remote. </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Nice!</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> We have pre rendered posts and comments. 🎉</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXd5hGPocQN6K2sjgqHiq8mpxKl_75Pq0WVDfqxR114klZVJcrO6-TjbB5GAnRTgRNbGlb869SwkzafTn1GGtTEStLtpCGo1xeMWxpnPvJ_DpxT0JEv_MeMolGCGe9aM2Eju1Vo0alW13w534Vr2ai9QpPAl?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="260" width="488"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Now we can do some tests. Delete the comments from the database and set your browser throttling to fast 3G.</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXeGVSR1q-3YlWoNGVhXmhSYwI3lQBx4vbyx7toFTiu2Sx3SbSU6AptNcQ4SWfAQOM0KCGEHHcgicZL-OZQb0Td3Eok-MFAQzAgHS8k6VR6IlXoMtdX9HGoS9f8mmEqOrm543ChGwAtUgp0b0jXsfTAZE1F4?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="386" width="472"></span></div><div></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">HANDLING HYDRATION ISSUES WITH @DEFER</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">As we can see, at the start our application displays old comments. Then, hydration kicks in and refreshes the comments. Comments are quite dynamic. We can rebuild the page after adding a post once a week, but rendering after each comment? - Bad idea.&nbsp;</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">How can we fix this?</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">We can use </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">@defer</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml">@defer { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">comments</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">comments</span>$]=<span class="hljs-string">"comments$()"</span> /&gt;</span> } </code></pre><div></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdWoNGn6-po6Y_-mpTfIJQl4sZDuXzrUbena6Oa31kEo33d5dhL7DzsmbBMZizQx8GyrG4kUWAIXQ2lUGb9ppiqDFXaPQoGbFjkrkqZ8oN5JOkWdFpxDZOG_Ub6E6-4YrVnL1SVqoUQ8BAyzXawyUHOEhw?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="386" width="472"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Not perfect, but there are some disadvantages when using SSG.</span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Update routes.txt with post IDs. The intention is to rebuild the app after adding a new blog post. So, it can be done manually for now. Maybe one of you has an idea on how this can be done automatically?</span></div><div></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">UPDATING ROUTES</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Let update </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">app.routes.ts</strong></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-attr">routes</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">Routes</span> = [ &nbsp;{ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">path</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''posts''</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">children</span>: readerRoutes, &nbsp;}, &nbsp;{ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">path</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''admin''</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">loadChildren</span>: <span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">import</span>(<span class="hljs-string">''./admin/admin.routes''</span>).<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function"><span class="hljs-params">r</span> =&gt;</span> r.<span class="hljs-property">adminRoutes</span>), &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">title</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''Admin''</span>, &nbsp;}, &nbsp;{ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">path</span>:<span class="hljs-string">''**''</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">redirectTo</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''posts''</span> &nbsp;}, ]; </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">By wildcard for redirect users to Posts List.&nbsp;</span></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">ADDING STYLES WITH TAILWIND</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">OK, we have the skeleton ready. Now let’s add some better UI for the reader and the admin.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">For the user interface, we’ll use Tailwind CSS, which I’ve never worked with before (this will be fun!). For the admin interface, we’ll use PrimeNG, which I’m quite familiar with.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Check out the</span><a href="https://tailwindcss.com/docs/guides/angular" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://tailwindcss.com/docs/guides/angular" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Tailwind CSS installation guide for Angular</a></u><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Here’s my config:</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-comment">/** <span class="hljs-doctag">@type</span> {<span class="hljs-type">import(''tailwindcss'').Config</span>} */</span> <span class="hljs-variable language_">module</span>.<span class="hljs-property">exports</span> = { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">content</span>: [ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-string">''./src/**/*.{html,ts}''</span>, &nbsp;], &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">theme</span>: { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">extend</span>: { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">colors</span>: { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">primary</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''#12372A''</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">secondary</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''#436850''</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">tertiary</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''#ADBC9F''</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">quaternary</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''#FBFADA''</span>, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}, &nbsp;}, &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">plugins</span>: [], }; </code></pre><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Let''s add some default buttons into </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">styles.scss</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">:</span></div><pre data-language="css"><code class="css"><span class="hljs-comment">/* You can add global styles to this file, and also import other style files */</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">@tailwind</span> base; <span class="hljs-keyword">@tailwind</span> components; <span class="hljs-keyword">@tailwind</span> utilities; <span class="hljs-comment">/* Base button */</span> <span class="hljs-selector-class">.btn</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">@apply</span> text-base font-medium rounded-lg p-<span class="hljs-number">3</span>; } <span class="hljs-comment">/* button primary */</span> <span class="hljs-selector-class">.btn--primary</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">@apply</span> bg-primary text-white; } <span class="hljs-comment">/* button secondary */</span> <span class="hljs-selector-class">.btn--secondary</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">@apply</span> bg-quaternary text-black; } <span class="hljs-comment">/* Hover effects */</span> <span class="hljs-selector-class">.btn--primary</span><span class="hljs-selector-pseudo">:hover</span>, <span class="hljs-selector-class">.btn--secondary</span><span class="hljs-selector-pseudo">:hover</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">@apply</span> shadow-lg -translate-y-<span class="hljs-number">0.5</span>; } </code></pre><div></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">PSEUDO PRESENTATIONAL (HYBRID) COMPONENTS</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Lets create a new folder inside reader/_components called: presentational-components</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">and inside:</span></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">ng g c -c OnPush postCard </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(212, 212, 212); background-color: transparent;">})</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">PostCardComponent</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-meta">@Input</span>() post!: <span class="hljs-title class_">Post</span>; &nbsp;<span class="hljs-meta">@Input</span>() first : <span class="hljs-built_in">boolean</span> = <span class="hljs-literal">false</span>; } </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">It will accept a post and first (later on we will think how to get rid of passing business logic by the </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">@Input()</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">, to not mix business logic with UI). The first card will take a little more space.</span></div><div></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">ngClass</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"first ? ''card-main'' : ''card-default''"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"post-card"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">ngClass</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"first ? ''flex flex-col lg:flex-row'' : ''''"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">img</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">src</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"post.image"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">alt</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"Post Image"</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">ngClass</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"first ? ''w-full lg:w-2/3'' : ''post-image''"</span> /&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">ngClass</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"first ? ''w-full lg:w-1/3 p-4'' : ''post-content''"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">h2</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"post-title"</span>&gt;</span>{{ post.title }}<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">h2</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"post-summary"</span>&gt;</span>{{ post.description }}<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">a</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">href</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"post.id"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"read-more"</span>&gt;</span>Read more<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">a</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> Inside posts-list.component.html we can add out component, remember to import it in ts <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;@for (item of posts$ | async; track item.id; let f = $first) { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">blog-post-card</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;[<span class="hljs-attr">post</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"item"</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;[<span class="hljs-attr">first</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"f"</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;[<span class="hljs-attr">ngClass</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"f ? ''col-span-1 md:col-span-2 lg:col-span-3'' : ''''"</span> /&gt;</span> &nbsp;} <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><div></div><div></div><pre data-language="css"><code class="css">* Import TailwindCSS */ <span class="hljs-keyword">@import</span> <span class="hljs-string">''tailwindcss/utilities''</span>; <span class="hljs-comment">/* Additional styles for the card component */</span> <span class="hljs-selector-class">.post-card</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">@apply</span> bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md overflow-hidden transition-transform transform <span class="hljs-attribute">hover</span>:scale-<span class="hljs-number">105</span>; } <span class="hljs-selector-class">.card-default</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">@apply</span> p-<span class="hljs-number">4</span>; &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attribute">width</span>: <span class="hljs-number">100%</span>; } <span class="hljs-selector-class">.card-main</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">@apply</span> <span class="hljs-attribute">lg</span>:p-<span class="hljs-number">6</span> <span class="hljs-attribute">lg</span>:col-span-<span class="hljs-number">3</span> <span class="hljs-attribute">lg</span>:row-span-<span class="hljs-number">1</span>; &nbsp;<span class="hljs-attribute">width</span>: <span class="hljs-number">100%</span>; } <span class="hljs-selector-class">.post-image</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">@apply</span> w-full h-<span class="hljs-number">48</span> object-cover; } <span class="hljs-selector-class">.post-content</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">@apply</span> p-<span class="hljs-number">4</span>; } <span class="hljs-selector-class">.post-title</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">@apply</span> text-xl font-bold text-gray-<span class="hljs-number">900</span>; } <span class="hljs-selector-class">.post-summary</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">@apply</span> text-gray-<span class="hljs-number">700</span>; } <span class="hljs-selector-class">.read-more</span> { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">@apply</span> text-primary <span class="hljs-attribute">hover</span>:underline; } </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">That looks nice!, especially considering it’s quite auto-generated by GTP with Tailwind.</span></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">DESIGN OVERVIEW</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Desktop view:</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdaT7LOdt3OS-1cbKkwwDjvU3Xx3s3hBPWFNATm-zKmgKYEjXZGoUh_N7DSWia5YaAFnXXGF968_utvcatgNN-Tj9WugYPXHDV05UG8MpnlvgplQyjDjOM1aYRYKaOpF9CVY4uTZmEQM7Tl47na0XCLGLTN?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="351" width="602"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Cards are responsive out of the box - that''s nice.</span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Mobile View:</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfb8iHU38beWAG15p50iKyQXPPfsDaCofnxWW4JJTRpvHZfNu5uMI6yos81es0vap2CAgptDGZ1yJtB_2RaForV2Uj2VO8MoBunX7LGXIpQ_PZrOTEJmmiSYWfiVqxYM9x_XkbCiJoKuofNG-IqU42_N2VS?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="875" width="570"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">I love my meaningful names!</span></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">TWEAKING STYLES&nbsp;</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Add some header with logo:</span></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">header</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"bg-primary h-[200px] flex lg:justify-center"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"lg:w-8/12 sm:w-8/12 sm:w-100 flex"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"flex row items-center"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">img</span> <span class="hljs-attr">src</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"logo_white_A.png"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">alt</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"Logo"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"h-36"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">h1</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"text-white lg:text-4xl md:text-2xl sm:text-xl font-bold"</span>&gt;</span>Welcome to Angular.fun<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">h1</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">h2</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"text-white lg:text-xl md:text-l sm:text-sm"</span>&gt;</span>Give fun back to coding<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">h2</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">header</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">OK, let’s move on to the Post page. We’ll keep it simple for now. For later, we’ll add some likes, shares, etc., but maybe in part 2. 😄</span></div><div></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml">@if (post$ | async; as post) { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">section</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"flex justify-center"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"w-full lg:w-6/12"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">img</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"w-full h-64 object-cover mt-10"</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">src</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"post.image"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">alt</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"{{ post.title }}"</span> /&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">h1</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"text-3xl font-bold text-center my-5"</span>&gt;</span>{{ post.title }}<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">h1</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"text-center text-gray-500"</span>&gt;</span>{{ post.author }} - {{ post.date | date }}<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-comment">&lt;!-- <span class="hljs-doctag">TODO:</span> Add social share buttons --&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"mt-4"</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">innerHTML</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"post.content"</span>&gt;</span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">add-comment</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">postId</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"id"</span> /&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;@defer { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;@if (comments$()) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">comments</span> *<span class="hljs-attr">ngIf</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"comments$()"</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">comments</span>$]=<span class="hljs-string">"comments$()"</span> /&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">section</span>&gt;</span> } </code></pre><div></div><div></div><div></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXf36aOTm8nTzZ2ILjLhm6vHQEibP10iKJxA_E5MYMCJSOcXm4N6EI8IBrhSO8-cIEn7jAi7XoH5aunIRjqb-FYl92kfmwcYqXKGqyBF-5KLOOk72B913WYF1raHWTvdIwrTtdtrTBRvlmEyWA9fuLM-8J1U?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="267" width="602"></span></div><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Looks fine, but text is too tight so lets loose density a little bit.</span></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"mt-4 leading-8"</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">innerHTML</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"post.content"</span>&gt;</span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Let set </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">leading-8</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> which is </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">line-height</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> 2 rem.</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> <img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdpTqXx3hptsX_tw6_ebBiIARtRgeJ32QLbKaWe0I97DPhx767PPpUrMzDBOicvpgFId9MsvwG9avqQRaoLFCEjwXlDTd4cQTSOPLd9I8DpkoTVe2cuUXtNz0qdRHBiZoNVnDEuY3DgtnVWC2w-jMrW6yG9?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="163" width="602"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">a lot better.</span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">We can jump into </span><strong>AddCommentComponent</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">,</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">lets generate HTML with ChatGpt: </span></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"mx-auto p-4 pt-5 bg-white shadow-md rounded-lg"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">h2</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4"</span>&gt;</span>Wht do you think?<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">h2</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">form</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">formGroup</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"commentForm"</span> (<span class="hljs-attr">ngSubmit</span>)=<span class="hljs-string">"onSubmit()"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"mb-4"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">textarea</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">id</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"content"</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">formControlName</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"content"</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"w-full p-3 border border-gray-300 rounded-md shadow-sm focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-green-950 focus:border-transparent"</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">rows</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"5"</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">placeholder</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"Write your comment here..."</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&gt;</span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">textarea</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"flex justify-end"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">button</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"btn btn--primary"</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;[<span class="hljs-attr">disabled</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"commentForm.invalid"</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Submit &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">button</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">form</span>&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">I made some modifications, but it still looks like a Bootstrap tutorial. I’m not a designer, but, still a better love story than Twilight. 😄</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfGJXZ9pDf34PR0NCeWJJmT8f4ykq8Hdx3i4F1P7hOBxJTS0mFXQRbPBLmQqonya4563u2cVhyS85XiFXGV_Hg1EQ_2WZDkPJI8kkeYwiBbBx9HwDFNG4Dd_P9f79EcQQ1qBAZjekpde4uMRu0LNlZ28UTU?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="249" width="602"></span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Later we’ll take care of error handling, but for now, we’re YOLO-ing it!</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">OK, let’s move on with CommentsComponent. We’ll use code from GPT again, polish it a bit with Copilot, and change the colors to match our palette. Great, looks fine!</span></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"comments-section"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">h2</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"text-xl font-semibold mb-4"</span>&gt;</span>Comments<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">h2</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;@for (comment of comments$(); track comment.id) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"comment mb-4 p-4 bg-tertiary bg-opacity-20 rounded-lg shadow-sm"</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"text-gray-800 mb-2"</span>&gt;</span>{{ comment.content }}<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"text-sm text-gray-600"</span>&gt;</span>- {{ comment.author }}<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">p</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><div></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">THE ADMIN SIDE WITH PRIMENG&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">We’re almost done with the Reader side, so let’s jump back to the Admin side.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">First of all, run:</span></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">npm install primeng </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Follow the</span><a href="https://primeng.org/installation" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://primeng.org/installation" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">PrimeNG installation guide</a></u><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> to configure it. We’ll be using the</span><a href="https://primeng.org/editor" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> </a><u style="color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent;"><a href="https://primeng.org/editor" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">PrimeNG editor</a></u><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">, so we need to install Quill as well.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Next, let’s go to the HTML view, remove the current control, and add the editor.</span></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml">@defer { <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">form</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">formGroup</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"blogForm"</span> (<span class="hljs-attr">ngSubmit</span>)=<span class="hljs-string">"onSubmit()"</span>&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">label</span> <span class="hljs-attr">for</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"title"</span>&gt;</span>Title:<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">label</span>&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">input</span> <span class="hljs-attr">id</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"title"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">formControlName</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"title"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">required</span>&gt;</span> @if (blogForm.get(''title'')?.invalid &amp;&amp; (blogForm.get(''title'')?.dirty || blogForm.get(''title'')?.touched)) { @if (blogForm.get(''title'')?.errors?.[''required'']) { <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span>Title is required.<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> } } <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">p-editor</span> <span class="hljs-attr">ngDefaultControl</span> <span class="hljs-attr">formControlName</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"content"</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">style</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"{ height: ''700px'' }"</span> /&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">button</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"btn btn--primary"</span> <span class="hljs-attr">type</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"submit"</span> [<span class="hljs-attr">disabled</span>]=<span class="hljs-string">"blogForm.invalid"</span>&gt;</span>Submit<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">button</span>&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">form</span>&gt;</span> } </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">In the component, we need to add </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">EditorModule</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> to the Imports array.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Next, we need to adjust our Post component to display HTML:</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-title function_">ngOnInit</span>(<span class="hljs-params"></span>) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">post$</span> = <span class="hljs-title function_">from</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">apiService</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">getPost</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">id</span>)) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;.<span class="hljs-title function_">pipe</span>( &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-title function_">map</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params"><span class="hljs-attr">post</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">Post</span> | <span class="hljs-literal">null</span></span>) =&gt;</span> { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (post) { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;post.<span class="hljs-property">content</span> = <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">sanitizer</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">bypassSecurityTrustHtml</span>(post.<span class="hljs-property">content</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">as</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span>); &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> post; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;); &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">comments$</span>! = <span class="hljs-title function_">runInInjectionContext</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">injector</span>, <span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">toSignal</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">apiService</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">getComments</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">id</span>))); &nbsp;} </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">There was a small issue with the list because of Tailwind. A small fix is needed in </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">styles.scss</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">. Maybe later, I will try to force the PrimeNG Editor to use Tailwind classes, but I think that might be tough. Alternatively, we can use</span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"> string.replace().</strong></div><pre data-language="css"><code class="css"><span class="hljs-keyword">@tailwind</span> base; <span class="hljs-keyword">@tailwind</span> components; <span class="hljs-keyword">@tailwind</span> utilities; <span class="hljs-keyword">@layer</span> base { &nbsp;<span class="hljs-selector-tag">ol</span>, <span class="hljs-selector-tag">ul</span> { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attribute">list-style</span>: initial; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attribute">padding-left</span>: <span class="hljs-number">40px</span>; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-attribute">margin</span>: <span class="hljs-number">1em</span> <span class="hljs-number">0</span>; &nbsp;} } </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">As we can see, primeNG converts images out of the box:&nbsp;</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdTd9LDe2J7rK41y_Sj7vc9vgrnfrJgVKB5D4lQieXwfpr-0ZiqoDMQKXoZC2k8Xtlcc7qI_QgiqG9E2RZBSHcCSdOYgNFoFlwI8hl43VgsPGWQCokvgON2tiDemSrkRLB7JIq0f_rK9eA8v1WBRYq3ilc?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="151" width="564"></span></div><div class="ql-align-center"></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">We are getting closer and closer to the end of this chapter.</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcQ7pTgLsM49MZtXav2EVnluDqVATWVxrxDgg1CvBUFvK3oTTeq8hosISPXjoEx3NOB357Taj9YracNXcITfhzbj9kBfnTSkZQVnVvYdcUlrqRvze7N1_jnkSdLLqZHCtXD8F5heUe95QmfnzpJ6F_Rbvlc?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="339" width="602"></span></div><div></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">SETTING UP FIREBASE AUTHENTICATION</span></h2><div class="ql-align-center"></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Maybe it’s not finished yet; we still have our database exposed for anyone to do anything. Let’s fix this. Go to the Firebase Console and from “Build,” choose “Authentication,” then click the “Get Started” button.</span></div><div></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdblLKI-9cn-IQCe5vtfODpCA38q6dxZAvAu0hsm23mKxeG1yogxbgkk0GCp-EDCgI8Wof980d46417h44ccLAtI_zZQ8sc9TJAimSjvluiEL7HgFPUHAUkb_J_1JZupZpXSi2luv6Zy1sOKmKbavP9BKZK?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="233" width="602"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Let’s choose </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Email/Password</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> and </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Google</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">, for now.&nbsp;</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">First option is quite easy to configure, the second also.</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcmLWcVLsFMTrBxUm9vEbb9Bnegmay6ARYDNlOybO2gjVraTlpr4E8Eoo9jB8iGG7jVZwk8bPrCp9YuTLahYiOCLiKRH9yBKhTVdCkAOVfoY-94o12eAzpSLEf-B2Msp8IxM9sObbYcPQbv7lplAUge7Pc?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="359" width="602"></span></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Go to </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Users</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> tab</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXeA44owvig3ZWXCb8E4asvEmJMVGUC4NxUy-HUXlrGxTiRzkt_IwJRHhfKSJNrAGo_4AbdkttAjlQzrgVrrTV3Iq8pLyYPeaIdBMXDHZU3-l60zuADhsYtVHJNQAz2rpgZBnUz-lGsOskWStN5GqviEghds?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="155" width="602"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Click ‘</span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Add user</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">’ and add your user.&nbsp;</span></div><div></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">APP AUTH</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Let’s add the auth folder in shared. And generate a </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">LoginComponent</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">, </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">RegisterComponent</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> and </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">AuthService</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">OK, this is our </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">AuthService</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> it was quite easy:</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { <span class="hljs-title class_">Injectable</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">WritableSignal</span>, inject, signal } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''@angular/core''</span>; <span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { <span class="hljs-title class_">Auth</span>, signInWithEmailAndPassword, signInWithPopup, <span class="hljs-title class_">GoogleAuthProvider</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">User</span>, createUserWithEmailAndPassword, onAuthStateChanged, <span class="hljs-title class_">IdTokenResult</span>, } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''@angular/fire/auth''</span>; <span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { <span class="hljs-title class_">Observable</span> } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''rxjs''</span>; <span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { <span class="hljs-title class_">Credentials</span> } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''../shared/_models/credentials.interface''</span>; <span class="hljs-meta">@Injectable</span>({ <span class="hljs-attr">providedIn</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''root''</span> }) <span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">AuthService</span> { <span class="hljs-attr">user$</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">WritableSignal</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-title class_">User</span> | <span class="hljs-literal">null</span>&gt; = <span class="hljs-title function_">signal</span>(<span class="hljs-literal">null</span>); <span class="hljs-attr">isAdmin$</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">WritableSignal</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-built_in">boolean</span>&gt; = <span class="hljs-title function_">signal</span>(<span class="hljs-literal">false</span>); <span class="hljs-keyword">private</span> auth = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">Auth</span>); <span class="hljs-keyword">private</span> provider = <span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">GoogleAuthProvider</span>(); <span class="hljs-title function_">loginWithEmail</span>(<span class="hljs-attr">credentials</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">Credentials</span>): <span class="hljs-title class_">Promise</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-built_in">void</span>&gt; { <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">signInWithEmailAndPassword</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">auth</span>, credentials.<span class="hljs-property">email</span>, credentials.<span class="hljs-property">password</span>).<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">userCredentials</span>) =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">user$</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">set</span>(userCredentials.<span class="hljs-property">user</span>); userCredentials.<span class="hljs-property">user</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">getIdTokenResult</span>().<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">idTokenResult</span>) =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">isAdmin$</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">set</span>(idTokenResult.<span class="hljs-property">claims</span>[<span class="hljs-string">''admin''</span>] <span class="hljs-keyword">as</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">boolean</span>); }); }) } <span class="hljs-comment">//Automaticly login user afrter registration is successful</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">registerWithEmail</span>(<span class="hljs-attr">credentials</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">Credentials</span>): <span class="hljs-built_in">void</span> { <span class="hljs-title function_">createUserWithEmailAndPassword</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">auth</span>, credentials.<span class="hljs-property">email</span>, credentials.<span class="hljs-property">password</span>).<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">userCredentials</span>) =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">user$</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">set</span>(userCredentials.<span class="hljs-property">user</span>); userCredentials.<span class="hljs-property">user</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">getIdTokenResult</span>().<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">idTokenResult</span>) =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">isAdmin$</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">set</span>(idTokenResult.<span class="hljs-property">claims</span>[<span class="hljs-string">''admin''</span>] <span class="hljs-keyword">as</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">boolean</span>); }); }); } <span class="hljs-title function_">loginGoogle</span>(): <span class="hljs-built_in">void</span> { <span class="hljs-title function_">signInWithPopup</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">auth</span>, <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">provider</span>) .<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">userCredentials</span>) =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">user$</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">set</span>(userCredentials.<span class="hljs-property">user</span>); userCredentials.<span class="hljs-property">user</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">getIdTokenResult</span>().<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">idTokenResult</span>) =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">isAdmin$</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">set</span>(idTokenResult.<span class="hljs-property">claims</span>[<span class="hljs-string">''admin''</span>] <span class="hljs-keyword">as</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">boolean</span>); }); }).<span class="hljs-title function_">catch</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">error</span>) =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-variable language_">console</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">error</span>(error); }) } <span class="hljs-title function_">logout</span>(): <span class="hljs-built_in">void</span> { <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">auth</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">signOut</span>().<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function">() =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">user$</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">set</span>(<span class="hljs-literal">null</span>); <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">isAdmin$</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">set</span>(<span class="hljs-literal">false</span>); }); } } </code></pre><div></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Dynamic Dialog</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Let’s generate ModalComponent with service in shared folder</span></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">ng g c -c OnPush dynamic-dialog </code></pre><div></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">ng g s dynamic-dialog </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">The idea is to create a shared, dynamic dialog where a component can be rendered dynamically.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Let’s create a service to handle this:</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { <span class="hljs-title class_">Injectable</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">EnvironmentInjector</span>, inject, <span class="hljs-title class_">ComponentRef</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">Type</span> } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''@angular/core''</span>; <span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { <span class="hljs-title class_">DynamicDialogComponent</span> } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''./dynamic-dialog.component''</span>; <span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { <span class="hljs-title class_">ViewContainerRef</span> } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''@angular/core''</span>; <span class="hljs-meta">@Injectable</span>({ <span class="hljs-attr">providedIn</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''root''</span> }) <span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">DynamicDialogService</span> { <span class="hljs-keyword">private</span> envInjector = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">EnvironmentInjector</span>); <span class="hljs-keyword">private</span> componentRef!: <span class="hljs-title class_">ComponentRef</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-title class_">DynamicDialogComponent</span>&gt;; openDialog&lt;C <span class="hljs-keyword">extends</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">Type</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-built_in">unknown</span>&gt;&gt;(<span class="hljs-attr">component</span>: C, <span class="hljs-attr">viewContainerRef</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">ViewContainerRef</span>): <span class="hljs-built_in">void</span> { <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">componentRef</span> = viewContainerRef.<span class="hljs-title function_">createComponent</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">DynamicDialogComponent</span>, { <span class="hljs-attr">environmentInjector</span>: <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">envInjector</span> }); <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">componentRef</span>.<span class="hljs-property">instance</span>.<span class="hljs-property">component</span> = component; }; <span class="hljs-title function_">closeDialog</span>(<span class="hljs-params"></span>) { <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">componentRef</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">destroy</span>(); }; } </code></pre><div></div><div></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { <span class="hljs-title class_">ChangeDetectionStrategy</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">Component</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">Input</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">OnInit</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">Type</span>, <span class="hljs-title class_">ViewContainerRef</span>, inject, viewChild } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''@angular/core''</span>; <span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { <span class="hljs-title class_">DynamicDialogService</span> } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''./dynamic-dialog.service''</span>; <span class="hljs-meta">@Component</span>({ <span class="hljs-attr">selector</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''app-dynamic-dialog''</span>, <span class="hljs-attr">standalone</span>: <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>, <span class="hljs-attr">imports</span>: [], <span class="hljs-attr">providers</span>: [], <span class="hljs-attr">templateUrl</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''./dynamic-dialog.component.html''</span>, <span class="hljs-attr">styleUrl</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''./dynamic-dialog.component.scss''</span>, <span class="hljs-attr">changeDetection</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">ChangeDetectionStrategy</span>.<span class="hljs-property">OnPush</span> }) <span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">DynamicDialogComponent</span>&lt;C = <span class="hljs-built_in">unknown</span>&gt; <span class="hljs-keyword">implements</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">OnInit</span> { <span class="hljs-meta">@Input</span>() component!: <span class="hljs-title class_">Type</span>&lt;C&gt;; divEl = viewChild.<span class="hljs-title function_">required</span>(<span class="hljs-string">''dynamicComponentContainer''</span>, { <span class="hljs-attr">read</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">ViewContainerRef</span> }); dynamicDialogService = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">DynamicDialogService</span>); viewContainerRef = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">ViewContainerRef</span>); <span class="hljs-title function_">ngOnInit</span>(): <span class="hljs-built_in">void</span> { <span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">divEl</span>()) { <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">divEl</span>().<span class="hljs-title function_">createComponent</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">component</span>); } } <span class="hljs-title function_">closeDialog</span>(<span class="hljs-params"></span>) { <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">dynamicDialogService</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">closeDialog</span>(); } } </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">In HTML we placing template, inside code generated by GPT:</span></div><pre data-language="xml"><code class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">div</span> <span class="hljs-attr">class</span>=<span class="hljs-string">"mt-2"</span>&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">ng-template</span> #<span class="hljs-attr">dynamicComponentContainer</span>&gt;</span><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">ng-template</span>&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">div</span>&gt;</span> </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">In </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Navbar</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> we just need to call&nbsp;</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-title function_">signIn</span>(<span class="hljs-params"></span>) { <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">dynamicDialogService</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">openDialog</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">LoginCompontent</span>, <span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">viewContainerRef</span>); }; </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">With component and </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">viewContainerRef</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">SETTING ADMIN CLAIMS</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">In AuthService we can see </span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">isAdmin$</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">set</span>(idTokenResult.<span class="hljs-property">claims</span>[<span class="hljs-string">''admin''</span>] <span class="hljs-keyword">as</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">boolean</span>); </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">We are setting the admin role based on whether the user has ‘admin’ claims (only at login for now; it’s not working on refresh yet due to a race condition issue). So, we need to set admin claims to true. Sounds easy? Yes! Will it be? Nope.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Ideally, this should be possible through Firestore or the Authentication GUI, but it isn’t. To set admin claims, we need to write a cloud function.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">What’s the catch? We can’t do this on the free version of Firebase. However, we still have some free limits within the paid plan, which is fair enough.</span></div><div></div><div></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXckzv3wkhZqInEp7rryvovtogx-hqabRG0YAlAQrYEmxhck4Nx07mmQHpTUVGqA63YW-_Sk01_Mjd1aVCl71CRcMJQVZMlV_Nlpm_BZlaZVXE61S6A5iw4x04zGr3uzjXSBhiYmpDD9Y-Icp1VlQgLu0btY?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="507" width="234"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Let’s get started with functions.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">First, install the Firebase tools:</span></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">npm install -g firebase-tools </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Then, initialize Firebase:</span></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">firebase init </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Choose “Functions: Configure a Cloud Functions directory and its files.”</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">We don’t need ESLint for now.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Select the project and language. We’ll choose </span><strong style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">TypeScript</strong><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">The wizard will add a new project called functions to our app. Additionally, the configurations will be updated.</span></div><div></div><div></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfiieBd38fK6LCibfk_C6Z2X6BvUz8xoXgusohMOy11QJci8Qgu9kWIgBSRry_2SEGpw8zlTM31FwOGVOxJE75bPwGP-JuDsTaHqib3WBMwhedfWZhO_W0Glwzcp6Ozd6xV7dDLrSOsxq1ZrmsvwRj7x2Tu?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="368" width="602"></span></div><div class="ql-align-center"></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">In our </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">index.ts</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"> we can write a method, looks like this.</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { initializeApp } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''firebase-admin/app''</span>; <span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> { getAuth } <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''firebase-admin/auth''</span>; <span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> * <span class="hljs-keyword">as</span> v2 <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">''firebase-functions/v2''</span>; <span class="hljs-title function_">initializeApp</span>(); <span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> setCustomUserClaims = v2.<span class="hljs-property">https</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">onRequest</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">request, response</span>) =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-keyword">debugger</span>; <span class="hljs-keyword">try</span> { <span class="hljs-title function_">getAuth</span>().<span class="hljs-title function_">getUserByEmail</span>(<span class="hljs-string">''lukasz,jablonski1991@gmail.con''</span>).<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">res</span>) =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-title function_">getAuth</span>().<span class="hljs-title function_">setCustomUserClaims</span>(res.<span class="hljs-property">uid</span>, { <span class="hljs-attr">admin</span>: <span class="hljs-literal">true</span> }).<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">res</span>) =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-variable language_">console</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">log</span>(<span class="hljs-string">''Admin role set successfully.''</span>, res); }); }); } <span class="hljs-keyword">catch</span> (error) { <span class="hljs-variable language_">console</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">error</span>(<span class="hljs-string">''Error setting custom claims:''</span>, error); response.<span class="hljs-title function_">status</span>(<span class="hljs-number">500</span>).<span class="hljs-title function_">json</span>({ <span class="hljs-attr">status</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''error''</span>, <span class="hljs-attr">message</span>: <span class="hljs-string">''Failed to set admin role.''</span> }); } }); </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">It will take a while.&nbsp;</span></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">✔&nbsp;functions[setCustomUserClaims(us-central1)] Successful update operation. Function URL (setCustomUserClaims(us-central1)): https://setcustomuserclaims-xxxxxxxx i&nbsp;functions: cleaning up build files... ⚠&nbsp;functions: Unhandled error cleaning up build images. This could result in a small monthly bill if not corrected. You can attempt to delete these images by redeploying or you can delete them manually at https://console.cloud.google.com/gcr/images/angularblog-267d7/us/gcf </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Oh no, my precious 10 PLN! I will lose it. 🙁</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXezgo_QgHTeU2ZpBJAty6dzv9-MrKAmwqpyk-I0LDN46BQVJubsLLtFn8Ni8bDMFyLZAJQlT8PHobH_6oPdltFwDaDskq9SG6nazTAvBncWCkfu9ku7PfGurCSWrfC6N-uYft7CdpsNGquD7E0rnW7-st9f?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="601" width="602"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">OK, that’s cringe as F.</span></div><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">We have an address, and we will use it only once to set ourselves as admin. So, we don’t need to implement it in Angular code; besides, it wouldn’t be safe. Copy and paste the link into your browser.</span></div><pre data-language="plain"><code class="plain">Internal Server Error - Nice, that’s what we were expecting :). Let’s check the logs: Firebase Logs Error: There is no user record corresponding to the provided identifier. </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(14, 14, 14); background-color: transparent;">Not the worst error. I put a comma instead of a dot in my email address and an “n” instead of “m”</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfTBIX_HhV77ho2BdNAHJqcJcNenCgpY9gJWnH12ccTVBKyEXWLnz0ovt1jtauEdHEbGQtjYWaYs4YpgObCuRvLTwJOfHLR1IhpB0zTHjLQrJ02uD6FkEz2iy5_1y9INBCTBlWlV-6JnKRt4-vzicmy-jo?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="908" width="602"></span></div><div></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript">{<span class="hljs-string">"status"</span>:<span class="hljs-string">"success"</span>,<span class="hljs-string">"message"</span>...}, </code></pre><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">that''s optimistic. Let’s check token on JWT.io&nbsp;</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdMyPuONvFPmMkqdsplZfFWwkDqnnV7BJerv4NR39iAOTbiDhBPHEltHv2zLbhQg78kNlUTUvlVR5xdaEyqZ2_3u0S5khUeMjJSd0TnPIJWJwTFVLY3FHQ85bFACqRmb5kh5hm-kwkOexQcTwOGFobMwD_5?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="112" width="486"></span></div><div></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">SECURE FIRESTORE</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Excellent, we have an admin user. We can now secure our DB.&nbsp;</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">In Rules, set:</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript">service cloud.<span class="hljs-property">firestore</span> { &nbsp;&nbsp;match /databases/{database}/documents { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-comment">// Match for all posts</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;match /post/{postId} { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-comment">// Allow read access to all documents</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;allow <span class="hljs-attr">read</span>: <span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-comment">// Allow write access to documents only if the user is an admin</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;allow <span class="hljs-attr">write</span>: <span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> request.<span class="hljs-property">auth</span>.<span class="hljs-property">token</span>.<span class="hljs-property">admin</span> == <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="hljs-comment">// Match for comments within posts</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;match /comment/{commentId} { &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;allow <span class="hljs-attr">read</span>: <span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;allow <span class="hljs-attr">create</span>: <span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;allow <span class="hljs-attr">update</span>: <span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;} &nbsp;&nbsp;} } </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Let’s create a new account. Sign in and try to add a Post at the admin side.</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfuWdPElrnzz5ie77v0GQ-e7gbhWWqYmwW216t2FRPhdJvZj1T9x_R6rf4_fHzKBP4B1H_XBOYal9K7cqyqmKCXP-uvEpTKADuNcC4DR7xfvGxEMyly_6Ba-ETLZzZlhbTmAyueT3WzxVbV305szMY803CH?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="55" width="602">&nbsp;</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">It returns the success… but DB was’t updated. I’m not sure if some clever person can use it for some injections.I think it is always better to operate on sensitive data at backend by cloud functions.</span></div><div></div><h2 class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">ADDING GUARDS TO APP</span></h2><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">At the end let’s add some </span><strong style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">guard</strong><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">.</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-attr">authGuard</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">CanMatchFn</span> = (): <span class="hljs-title class_">Observable</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-built_in">boolean</span>&gt; =&gt; { <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> authService = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">AuthService</span>); <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> router = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">Router</span>); <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> authService.<span class="hljs-title function_">getAdminStatus</span>().<span class="hljs-title function_">pipe</span>( <span class="hljs-title function_">map</span>(<span class="hljs-function"><span class="hljs-params">isAdmin</span> =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (!isAdmin) { router.<span class="hljs-title function_">navigate</span>([<span class="hljs-string">''/posts''</span>]); } <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> isAdmin; }), <span class="hljs-title function_">take</span>(<span class="hljs-number">1</span>) ); }; </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Everything is working, we got stable and working pre-alpha version, with mixed messed styles and quite dope performance:</span></div><div class="ql-align-center"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;"><img src="https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXftwUcB67RcfbhJwp91725PmGg9IAa7T-wGhPSiis_CujKWPHHNWKD9INpqqs_Bh6EI6D35bBZO0AwosXdMeer5VAcdHNjVwV3nLohIAHqhSvr6P01ARc8PoHxjll91PHAhZm4qQtJX7iRJ5mGnwE7eziSw?key=gSl3PD129Of5xeoxs5pdzw" height="107" width="602"></span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">That’s nice. In the next chapter we will try to get 100% in SEO and keep performance even better, there still is CLS when there are images in posts.&nbsp;</span></div><div></div><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Little errata I caught that Firebase clearing </span><strong style="background-color: transparent;">Auth.currentUser</strong><span style="background-color: transparent;"> </span><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">after refresh. Our </span><strong style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">isAdmin$()</strong><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> also will be cleared as it is just a simple signal working only after login. We can use info stored in the </span><strong style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">onAuthStateChanged</strong><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(220, 220, 170);"> </span><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">method. So we can modify our </span><strong style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">AuthService</strong><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> and guard to be sure we are using the current </span><strong style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">User</strong><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> value.&nbsp;</span></div><div></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-title function_">getAdminStatus</span>(): <span class="hljs-title class_">Observable</span> &lt; <span class="hljs-built_in">boolean</span> &gt; { <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">Observable</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">observer</span>) =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-title function_">onAuthStateChanged</span>(<span class="hljs-variable language_">this</span>.<span class="hljs-property">auth</span>, <span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">user</span>) =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (user) { user.<span class="hljs-title function_">getIdTokenResult</span>().<span class="hljs-title function_">then</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params"><span class="hljs-attr">idTokenResult</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">IdTokenResult</span></span>) =&gt;</span> { observer.<span class="hljs-title function_">next</span>(idTokenResult.<span class="hljs-property">claims</span>[<span class="hljs-string">''admin''</span>] <span class="hljs-keyword">as</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">boolean</span>); observer.<span class="hljs-title function_">complete</span>(); }).<span class="hljs-title function_">catch</span>(<span class="hljs-function">(<span class="hljs-params">error</span>) =&gt;</span> { observer.<span class="hljs-title function_">error</span>(error); }); } <span class="hljs-keyword">else</span> { observer.<span class="hljs-title function_">next</span>(<span class="hljs-literal">false</span>); observer.<span class="hljs-title function_">complete</span>(); } }); }); } </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Not perfect code but working. I think we can move it to the app initializer in next chapters.&nbsp;</span></div><pre data-language="typescript"><code class="typescript"><span class="hljs-keyword">export</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-attr">authGuard</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">CanMatchFn</span> = (): <span class="hljs-title class_">Observable</span>&lt;<span class="hljs-built_in">boolean</span>&gt; =&gt; { <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> authService = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">AuthService</span>); <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> router = <span class="hljs-title function_">inject</span>(<span class="hljs-title class_">Router</span>); <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> authService.<span class="hljs-title function_">getAdminStatus</span>().<span class="hljs-title function_">pipe</span>( <span class="hljs-title function_">map</span>(<span class="hljs-function"><span class="hljs-params">isAdmin</span> =&gt;</span> { <span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (!isAdmin) { router.<span class="hljs-title function_">navigate</span>([<span class="hljs-string">''/posts''</span>]); } <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> isAdmin; }), <span class="hljs-title function_">take</span>(<span class="hljs-number">1</span>) ); }; </code></pre><div></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">So thank you for your time. Sorry that in some places I made a mess, I tried to show some real live coding. I know that code is not perfect, yet 😀. But maybe it will help you with something. I was learning by myself during this article. Made a few mistakes, a few temporary solutions. I haven''t tracked the time spent on writing that post, however I think it took around 50-60h with adding screens and editing text. I’ve spent quite a lot of time on some bugs I mentioned. Everything would take me about 45 minutes in WordPress, but would I have some fun during it? I don''t think so.&nbsp;</span></div><div><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;">Cheers and have fun with your coding!&nbsp;</span></div>
', false, '2024-06-29T22:00:00+00:00', 'https://aqdbdmepncxxuanlymwr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/covers/ChatGPT%20Image%2011%20sie%202026,%2020_53_29.png', '[]'::jsonb),
  ('9a3cf18d-d670-4954-beb6-53e3a21c9ee6', 'a3b3cf93-6956-41c7-bec0-13f95dd42f26', 'Super performant Blog app in Angular 19 (18) with SSG SSR and Hydration — Part 4: Move to Cloud and setup CI/CD with Github Actions', 'In this chapter, I set up GitHub Actions to deploy my Angular blog to Cloud Run using a JSON key. I ran into a bunch of permission issues, fixed them step by step, and finally got the deployment working. I added unit tests to block bad deploys, and a PR check workflow for better control. It’s now running smoothly, and I’m ready for the next step.', '<div>Today we will configure GCL and Github Actions.</div><div></div><div>To be honest, we will not move to the cloud. Cloud Run is used by Firebase App Hosting under the hood, so we will just do it manually to get more control. </div><div></div><div>Ok, let''s get started:</div><div></div><h2>Configure Google Cloud</h2><div></div><div>Switch to current project</div><pre data-language="plain">gcloud config set project YOUR_PROJECT_ID
</pre><div class="ql-align-center"></div><div>Enable <strong>the Artifact Registry API, Cloud Run API,</strong> <strong>IAM Credentials API, and IAM Service Account Credentials API.</strong></div><pre data-language="plain">gcloud services enable \
  run.googleapis.com \
  artifactregistry.googleapis.com \
  iamcredentials.googleapis.com \
  iam.googleapis.com \
  --project=supple-fold-455911-v2
</pre><div></div><div class="ql-align-center"></div><div>Create and configure an authentication for GitHub:</div><div>We have three options to choose <a href="https://github.com/google-github-actions/auth" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">docs</a>:</div><ol><li><u style="background-color: transparent; color: var(--fgColor-accent, var(--color-accent-fg));"><a href="https://github.com/google-github-actions/auth#direct-wif" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">(Preferred) Direct Workload Identity Federation</a></u></li><li><u style="background-color: transparent; color: var(--fgColor-accent, var(--color-accent-fg));"><a href="https://github.com/google-github-actions/auth#indirect-wif" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Workload Identity Federation through a Service Account</a></u></li><li><u style="background-color: transparent; color: var(--fgColor-accent, var(--color-accent-fg));"><a href="https://github.com/google-github-actions/auth#sake" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Service Account Key JSON</a></u></li></ol><div>To be honest, throughout my ambitions I chose the preferred option, but it failed a few times. There were authorization issues, and the docs are quite big. I dug and dug but haven''t found a solution. I took a look on the internet and see that people use JSON. I read about it. I found that it''s quite secure; yeah, you can lose your file, and someone can hack your GH account, but if someone were to hack your account, you''d be cooked anyway.</div><div>JSON is stored in GH credentials, so I''ll sleep well; I have nothing to lose ($10). To be honest, if someday I want to use this way of managing my CI/CD, I''ll definitely read all documentations and choose Direct Workload Identity Federation. Yeah, I have limited time; I''m working for free here.</div><div></div><div>The docs have only three steps:</div><div class="ql-align-center"><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></div><div class="ql-align-center"></div><div></div><div>Yeah, I was thinking, That''s it? Nope, it doesn''t.</div><div></div><div>OK, I''ll go now step by step through what I did. With all my failings as always xD</div><div></div><pre data-language="plain">gcloud iam service-accounts create github-deploy \
  --description="Konto do CI/CD z GitHub Actions" \
  --display-name="GitHub Deploy SA"
</pre><div></div><pre data-language="plain">export PROJECT_ID="supple-fold-455911-v2"
export SA_EMAIL="github-deploy@$PROJECT_ID.iam.gserviceaccount.com"

# Cloud Run Admin
gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding $PROJECT_ID \
  --member="serviceAccount:$SA_EMAIL" \
  --role="roles/run.admin"

# Artifact Registry Writer
gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding $PROJECT_ID \
  --member="serviceAccount:$SA_EMAIL" \
  --role="roles/artifactregistry.writer"

# IAM Service Account User
gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding $PROJECT_ID \
  --member="serviceAccount:$SA_EMAIL" \
  --role="roles/iam.serviceAccountUser"
</pre><div></div><pre data-language="plain">gcloud iam service-accounts keys create key.json \
  --iam-account "$SA_EMAIL"
</pre><div></div><div>Ok, here we have our JSON.</div><div></div><h2><strong>Configure Github</strong></h2><div></div><div>Serrings -&gt; Secrets and Variables (at left) -&gt; Actions -&gt; Selected action -&gt; New repository secret. Name will be <strong style="color: rgb(31, 35, 40); background-color: rgba(129, 139, 152, 0.1);">GCP_SA_KEY</strong><span style="color: rgb(31, 35, 40); background-color: rgba(129, 139, 152, 0.1);">. Just paste all JSON file content. </span><strong style="color: rgb(31, 35, 40); background-color: rgba(129, 139, 152, 0.1);">Voilà.</strong><span style="color: rgb(31, 35, 40); background-color: rgba(129, 139, 152, 0.1);"> (YEAH XD)</span></div><div></div><div>OK, so now we can. Set up our action; it''s my final version, but it still has some echos for fucking debug.</div><pre data-language="plain">name: Deploy Angular Blog to Cloud Run

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main  # or any other branch you use for production

jobs:
  deploy:
    name: Build and Deploy
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v3

      - name: Set up Node.js
        uses: actions/setup-node@v3
        with:
          node-version: ''18''

      - name: Install dependencies
        run: npm ci

      - name: Build Angular app
        run: npm run build --prod

      - name: Authenticate to Google Cloud
        uses: google-github-actions/auth@v2
        with:
          credentials_json: ''${{ secrets.GCP_SA_KEY }}''

      - name: Install Google Cloud SDK
        run: |
          echo "Installing Google Cloud SDK"
          echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/cloud.google.gpg] http://packages.cloud.google.com/apt cloud-sdk main" | sudo tee -a /etc/apt/sources.list.d/google-cloud-sdk.list
          sudo apt-get install -y apt-transport-https ca-certificates
          sudo apt-get update &amp;&amp; sudo apt-get install -y google-cloud-sdk
          gcloud version

      - name: Deploy to Cloud Run using Buildpacks
        uses: google-github-actions/deploy-cloudrun@v2
        with:
          service: angular-blog  # your Cloud Run service name
          region: europe-central2  # match to your region
          source: .
</pre><div></div><h2>Test deploy and fixes for Google Cloud</h2><div></div><div>OK! Let''s run.</div><pre data-language="plain">2025-04-05T12:25:17.9212605Z ##[group]Run google-github-actions/deploy-cloudrun@v2
